cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  stratigraphic-geochron: joint posterior ages for stratigraphically
  bracketed events
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. Please also cite the
  calibration curve and the calibration library listed under references.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Andrew D.
    family-names: Wickert
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9545-3365"
abstract: >-
  Combines the three kinds of geochronological constraint on a stratigraphic
  event – dates below the bed, which bound it as younger; dates above, which
  bound it as older; and dates on the bed itself – into a single Bayesian
  posterior. Limiting dates enter as survival and cumulative functions and
  dates on the bed as likelihoods, so the result is a product rather than a
  summed probability density. Radiocarbon ages are calibrated against IntCal20
  and luminescence ages treated as Gaussians, all on a shared calendar-age
  grid. Ships with a synthetic demonstration dataset and a four-panel figure
  that puts time on the vertical axis, so the plot reads like a core.
repository-code: "https://github.com/MNiMORPH/stratigraphic-geochron"
license: GPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - geochronology
  - radiocarbon calibration
  - IntCal20
  - luminescence dating
  - Bayesian age model
  - stratigraphy
  - terminus post quem
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Reimer
        given-names: Paula J.
    title: >-
      The IntCal20 Northern Hemisphere radiocarbon age calibration curve
      (0-55 cal kBP)
    journal: Radiocarbon
    volume: "62"
    year: 2020
    doi: 10.1017/RDC.2020.41
    notes: >-
      Reimer et al.; the full author list is given in the curve file shipped
      with iosacal. Used here for all radiocarbon calibration.
  - type: software
    authors:
      - family-names: Costa
        given-names: Stefano
    title: "IoSACal: open source radiocarbon calibration"
    repository-code: "https://codeberg.org/steko/iosacal"
    notes: Performs the IntCal20 calibration called by agedist.calibrate_14c.
